WEBVTT

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.640
My right hand holds a bowl of gold,

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:20.180
And my left holds one of silver.

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:24.720
Never one without the other,

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:37.800
Two unseen bowls for each of us.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:46.210
The golden one is filled with joy,

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:53.550
shining warmly.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:58.350
Since we met, my golden bowl

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:05.360
cannot hold all my happiness and love.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:15.500
Golden joy, silver sadness,

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:22.850
I would leave my past behind...

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.580
For you, for the sake of love,

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.520
I would empty the bowls of my past.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.190
I'm back...

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:09.730
Welcome home.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:10.990
Where's Dad?

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:12.530
He's not home yet...

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:18.130
Oh, Nanako-san, there's a letter for you...

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.800
Let's see... it's from Henmi-san...

00:02:21.940 --> 00:02:24.870
What! Really? Thank-you!

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:31.150
Wow! A big envelope! I wonder what it is.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:37.020
Dear Nanako-san, how have you been?

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.960
First, I must apologize for not writing very often...

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:46.700
I'm enclosing the brochure for our Gakuin University Fair.

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.300
Please take a look at it,

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:53.370
...and if it appeals to you, please do plan to attend.

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:56.910
There aren't any formal invitations,

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:59.510
...in fact, they told us to invite all the women we can!

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:05.310
I heard a rumor that there are prizes for all the women.

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:09.790
So please bring your friends.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.320
P.S.--

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:22.130
P.S. These days, I don't hear from you quite as often.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.800
I assume "no news is good news".

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:28.670
So I'm happy you're doing well.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:50.490
<b>20. The Gardening Shears</b>

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:56.300
Well, there are clubs for English, comedy, anime...

00:03:56.300 --> 00:03:59.500
Wow! All kinds of music ensembles too!

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.570
There's lots of food stands, also...

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.370
Let's go! Mariko-san will want to go too, I bet!

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:05.240
Sure!

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.780
Oh, look, look!

00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.910
There's a masquerade dance too!

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:16.390
You'd be wearing a mask. Then you could even hold hands in public!

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:19.920
"There are many masks to choose from"...

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.930
I'll take this one, "Snow White".

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.260
How about you? <b> </b>

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:26.730
How about you? This one, "Juliet".

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:29.460
Woo-woo! Then you'll meet a "Romeo"!!

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:38.070
The University Fair? There's a dance party?

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:41.080
How utterly disgusting!

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:43.280
Why? What's so disgusting about that?

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:45.410
The whole thing!

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:48.820
A man and woman holding hands, bodies touching...

00:04:48.820 --> 00:04:51.090
Just thinking about it gives me the creeps!

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:52.490
You're twisted!

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:54.560
Who's twisted?

00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:59.830
Anyway, I can't let you go to such a repulsive affair alone!

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:01.300
Mariko-san!

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.500
Give me back that program!!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:07.570
Geez! Hey, hold up!

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:09.040
Now see here...!!

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.710
Shinobu-san!

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:13.240
Hey! Give it back! That's Nanako's!

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.710
Is this program that important?

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:16.780
Of course!

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:19.520
Is it true, Nanako? <b> </b>

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:20.580
Is it true, Nanako? What?

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:23.120
That you're dating a boy?

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:25.050
That he's a student at Gakuin?

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:26.460
Shinobu-san!

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.460
I told you not to!

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:35.400
Now listen. This guy is like a brother to Nanako.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.930
It's not like he's her...

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:39.870
"LIKE" a brother, right? Not actually her brother, right?

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.740
What are you thinking about?

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.540
What business is it of YOURS who she associates with?

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.480
Well well! Now it's OBVIOUS that something's happening!

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.010
Can you believe this?

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.550
You won't catch me hanging out with you anymore!

00:05:53.150 --> 00:05:55.020
Let's go, Nanako.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.350
There's no point in asking her to go with us...

00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:01.360
...'cause she can't stand being near "disgusting" places!

00:06:01.490 --> 00:06:02.760
But...

00:06:03.290 --> 00:06:04.630
Just watch.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:05.830
What?

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:10.500
I... I'm coming!!

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:12.230
See?

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:15.570
It's just too big a risk for you two to go alone.

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:17.640
It's far too dangerous!

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:20.110
I have to protect Misonoo-san from the hands of men.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:23.050
That's OK. I'll protect her!

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:26.250
So, what time? And where do we meet?

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:36.530
My dear Brother,

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:41.460
...everyone is looking forward to the Fair this Sunday!

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.810
Professor Takada's "International Relations"

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:54.080
Don't worry, I have that book too...

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:58.880
Thanks! I've looked all over, but it's out of print.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:02.350
I can't sell it to you, but you can borrow it as long as you like...

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:03.820
But don't lose it.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.420
Alright.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:11.960
The brakes don't feel quite right.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:24.840
Go ahead. You know where my room is?

00:07:24.970 --> 00:07:25.970
Yeah, sure.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:28.240
Go on in while I check these out...

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:52.400
Oh, Fukiko-san... It's been a while! How are you?

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:55.540
Taking care of the roses?

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:57.610
Yes...

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:01.210
Your roses are always so gorgeous.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:07.280
Ouch!

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:13.490
Sorry... not very talkative, is she...

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:17.290
She must not like me.

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:19.500
Hah. Who knows.

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:25.370
When I first met her she was in grade school.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:29.910
Now she's a lovely young woman. Amazing!

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:32.770
I bet she's an alien.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.580
Whatever goes on in her head, it's a complete mystery to me.

00:08:35.910 --> 00:08:37.850
There we go! Got it!

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:47.520
Have a seat!

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.590
Why not join us for dinner?

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:54.260
No, no thanks. I have things to do.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:58.930
You know, you haven't been here since you graduated!

00:08:59.130 --> 00:09:01.670
Oh, I guess you're right.

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:07.340
By the way, did you invite your high-schooler to the fair?

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:11.010
Yes, I sent her a program.

00:09:11.080 --> 00:09:14.220
She said she's coming, and plans to bring a couple of friends.

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:18.750
Great! Girls usually enjoy university fairs.

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:30.970
Bye!

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:32.430
See you later...

00:09:56.660 --> 00:10:01.600
<i>Yoshino naru, natsumi no kawano kawa yodo ni, kamo no naku naru yamakage ni shite...</i>

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:05.270
What focused vision this poem has!

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.540
It is so suggestive, idyllic, and eloquent.

00:10:07.540 --> 00:10:08.140
Note the many "N" syllables used in it... <b> </b>

00:10:08.140 --> 00:10:12.140
Note the many "N" syllables used in it... I have a great idea!

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:14.010
It might have been too plain without that <b> </b>

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:17.080
It might have been too plain without that I don't think it's gonna work.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:19.740
You'll never know unless you try.

00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:22.550
Hey, over there! What's going on?

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:29.220
And ending that as "yamakage ni shite" is so suggestive, so...

00:10:35.420 --> 00:10:37.900
Excuse me, Kaoru-no-Kimi...?

00:10:44.310 --> 00:10:48.330
Saint-Juste-sama... I have a message for you.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.530
A message?

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:53.140
Yes, on behalf of Misonoo Nanako-san.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:54.560
A message?

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:57.170
Yes, on behalf of Mariko-san.

00:10:57.170 --> 00:11:00.120
Mariko-san would like you to come to the fair.

00:11:00.430 --> 00:11:02.980
The University Fair? Tomorrow?

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:08.900
We'd love to have you and Kaoru-no-Kimi go with us,

00:11:08.900 --> 00:11:11.640
So, here I am asking you for her,

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:15.190
...and Nanako-san is asking Kaoru-no-Kimi for me.

00:11:15.860 --> 00:11:18.940
Asking Kaoru to go to a fair at Gakuin University...

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:24.270
What? Um... but what's so funny about that?

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:30.270
The odds are probably ten thousand to one. There's no way she'll go.

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:32.280
Why not?

00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:34.070
Best you don't know why.

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:39.430
Also... I appreciate the offer, but I can't go either.

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:41.170
The Gakuin Fair?

00:11:41.590 --> 00:11:48.690
Yes... I know a graduate student there... so...

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:54.520
I'm sorry... we have another scrimmage on Sunday.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:58.390
Really? Mariko-san will miss you.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:11:59.530
Sorry!

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:09.430
I can forget, because I love.

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.580
I can forget, because I loved.

00:12:20.440 --> 00:12:22.180
Here's some tea...

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.060
Good, thanks.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:27.110
Did Nanako go to bed?

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:29.790
Not a chance.

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:35.310
Hey, look, Mom!

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:39.390
Don't you think the pearls would go perfectly with this dress?

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:41.540
Maybe, who knows...

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:43.620
For sure it would!

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:46.300
So, would you lend them to me, please?

00:12:46.440 --> 00:12:49.990
But it's only a university fair! Why a necklace?

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:52.070
Please! Just one day!

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:53.810
Well, if you insist.

00:12:54.010 --> 00:12:55.150
Thank you!

00:12:55.780 --> 00:12:57.390
In the upstairs dresser, right?

00:12:59.820 --> 00:13:01.830
Walking on air, isn't she?

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.110
Yes...

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:10.720
I wonder how she feels about Takehiko-san...

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:14.790
We should let her know soon.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:16.040
But...

00:13:17.890 --> 00:13:18.970
Don't worry.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:21.900
I'm not brave enough for that yet.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:27.080
But I know I'll have to, someday.

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:39.650
OK! All right!

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:49.560
Yes, Misonoo residence...

00:13:57.800 --> 00:14:03.160
I'm sorry to call so late. I have a favor to ask.

00:14:03.780 --> 00:14:05.060
Miya-sama?

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:08.430
Do you have any plans for tomorrow?

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:11.310
Um... tomorrow?

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.650
Yes, Sunday.

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:18.890
Well... yes. In the afternoon... with Shinobu-san.

00:14:19.220 --> 00:14:24.780
Oh good! Could you spare some time in the morning?

00:14:24.900 --> 00:14:26.440
Well... sure!

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:35.050
A tea ceremony?

00:14:36.460 --> 00:14:40.550
Yes! I have a tea ceremony every Sunday morning,

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:43.700
...and I invite one of the Sorority members.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:49.400
It seems everyone is busy tomorrow... so I'd like to invite you.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:54.210
So, would you? Come to my house tomorrow?

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:59.320
All right, I'll be free tomorrow morning.

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:01.200
I'm very grateful for the invitation.

00:15:01.340 --> 00:15:05.830
Thank goodness! I'm sure it will be lovely, just you and me.

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:07.800
Thank you, Nanako-san.

00:15:08.200 --> 00:15:10.150
You're welcome!

00:15:10.620 --> 00:15:11.700
Also...

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:12.500
Yes?

00:15:12.630 --> 00:15:15.780
Please don't mention this to anyone.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:16.870
Why?

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:20.890
This is the first time I've invited a freshman to a tea ceremony.

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:25.380
You understand. Some others might feel jealous about that.

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:27.410
OK, I understand.

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:29.820
Then, good night.

00:15:29.960 --> 00:15:32.700
Thank you very much. And good night.

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:51.900
I'm sorry, I forgot to tell you something!

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:59.380
Before you come over to my house, could you stop at the Sorority?

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:00.520
OK!

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:06.120
You know the storage room there? Please pick up the <i>Meissen</i> tea set.

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:08.830
The <i>Meissen</i> tea set?

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:13.590
Yes... a special set just for special guests.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:17.040
I'd like to use it for our ceremony tomorrow.

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:19.340
Well...

00:16:20.660 --> 00:16:23.750
The key is at the security desk.

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:26.430
Sorority members can always pick it up from there.

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:29.000
OK. All right.

00:16:30.770 --> 00:16:31.710
Bye, now....

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:48.620
See you then!

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:51.770
One o'clock sharp at Reuben's, in front of the university. OK?

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:53.850
OK. Be on time!

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:55.880
It should be OK.

00:16:55.880 --> 00:16:58.890
If the tea ceremony finishes by 11:30; I can make it...

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:06.330
The key to the Sorority's storage room?

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:09.010
Yes, it's right here.

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:12.220
Sign your name and grade.

00:17:12.690 --> 00:17:15.040
You're a member of the sorority, right?

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:16.860
Yes, I am.

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:36.870
There it is.

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:59.350
Now let's see... a <i>Meissen</i> tea set...

00:18:01.750 --> 00:18:05.840
This one... is a <i>Seiburu</i> soup set...

00:18:06.350 --> 00:18:10.370
They're all in boxes which look alike!

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:20.050
This is beyond me... I should have gotten more details...

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:38.100
It's locked! How on earth...?

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:52.540
That's strange. The door couldn't have locked itself!

00:18:53.150 --> 00:18:56.430
Who's there? Who locked the door?

00:18:59.030 --> 00:19:01.780
Open the door!! Stop playing games!!

00:19:02.210 --> 00:19:04.220
Please! I know you're there!

00:19:04.710 --> 00:19:06.850
Open the door! Please, open the door!

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:09.070
Please! I beg you!

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:14.400
Who's doing this? Open up! Please open the door!

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:19.010
What can I do now?

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:20.890
If I stay locked up in here,

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:23.900
...I'll miss the tea ceremony AND the university fair...!

00:19:27.990 --> 00:19:29.870
I knew it! There's someone out there!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:33.690
Wait! Don't go!! Help me, please!

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:35.430
Let me out!

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:38.840
Please!

00:19:57.150 --> 00:19:59.360
Stay there until evening.

00:20:17.730 --> 00:20:18.800
Sorry I'm late. <b> </b>

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:20.540
Sorry I'm late. Hi, Tomoko-san!

00:20:20.820 --> 00:20:23.840
I was afraid you were all waiting for me,

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:25.310
...but Nanako still isn't here?

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.890
Give her 5 more minutes...

00:20:28.950 --> 00:20:32.300
Hey, let's charge her 100 Yen for each minute!

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:34.050
It's a deal!

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:46.480
My dear Brother, I'm sorry.

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:49.130
It looks like I won't be at the fair.

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:57.750
And how will I be able to apologize to Miya-sama?

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:17.990
You're working far too hard for a Sunday!

00:21:21.520 --> 00:21:25.940
And you? You're smoking far too much for a Sunday!

00:21:27.280 --> 00:21:30.760
I'd promise to quit smoking.

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:34.310
...if you went to the Gakuin University Fair.

00:21:56.060 --> 00:21:57.330
Her program...!

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:13.610
So, I'll have a little fair just for me...

00:22:53.290 --> 00:22:56.100
Miss Fukiko, there's a phone call...

00:22:56.230 --> 00:22:58.650
...it's from Misonoo-san...

00:22:58.850 --> 00:22:59.850
What?

00:23:00.450 --> 00:23:03.530
I'm very sorry. I can't apologize enough.

00:23:03.850 --> 00:23:08.670
Kaoru-no-Kimi broke the lock and then she...

00:23:08.960 --> 00:23:12.040
I can't believe this happened! I'm sorry I missed everything.

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:16.930
Really? I had no idea. What an experience!

00:23:17.170 --> 00:23:20.920
We'll have the tea ceremony some other time.

00:23:21.160 --> 00:23:26.590
Don't keep Shinobu-san and the others waiting. Enjoy the fair.

00:23:27.060 --> 00:23:30.010
Oh really? Really?

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:34.450
Of course, enjoy it! Have fun.

00:23:35.560 --> 00:23:36.970
Thank you!

00:24:10.160 --> 00:24:14.360
I dreamed I was chasing a rainbow...

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:19.830
Then the rainbow I was chasing was you.

00:24:21.300 --> 00:24:25.440
Before, I had no strength, no will.

00:24:25.440 --> 00:24:30.910
But now because of you, I do.

00:24:31.650 --> 00:24:37.190
Feelings of love, like raindrops

00:24:37.190 --> 00:24:42.660
Come pouring from the sky.

00:24:42.660 --> 00:24:45.390
This is surely a game

00:24:45.390 --> 00:24:48.200
